{
  "dom_id": "question-132775",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "The velocity of the particle in the $y$-direction when $t=2$ is equal to the rate of change of the particle's $y$-coordinate at this time. Calculate this velocity.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The velocity of the particle in the $y$-direction when $t=2$ second equals\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.$",
  "worked_solution": "The rate of change of the particle's $y$-coordinate when $t=2$ is given by ${y}^{′}(2).$\n\nIn step 5, we found that\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{3-3{t}^{2}}{t({t}^{2}+3)}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $t=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(2) & =\\frac{3-3(2)^{2}}{2({2}^{2}+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-12}{2(7)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{14}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
